A||N||15||Chance||86GT 5speed clutch problems FINALLY SOLVED!!!||||4||
Z||000000||Chance||03-16-2001||01:04 AM||||Well, after a year or so of ALL my clutch problems, I HOPE NOW, that they are over.  (long story most of you old timers already know) <BR>     To be as brief as possible, 2 1/2 years ago, clutch "blew/shattared" Took to place I trusted with previous cars, got new clutch, new flywheel (said old one was too burned) new clutch master cyl (bent rod).  1200 bucks later, it worked somewhat decently I guess, but a few months later, it wouldn't engage when I pressed pedal.  I bled the slave, and it seemed to be O.k. so I didn't think anything else... month or so later, same thing. Happend on the way back from Dallas, I thought it was just because I was driving so long without having to shift, it may of just lost pressure, so, I bled it in a parking lot between there and home.  Didn't quite shift well, but I could somewhat "pump it up"  and get by.  Well, I got home, bled again, and just when to bed, next day, worked great. till i drove around a while, then it would not shift, then sometimes if I stoped to get gas, or a soda, get back in...worked again!!!  by the time it got to the point where I couldn't shift, it was a little over a year since I  had it put in.  But I thought it was just the slave, so I bled, and it would kind of work, so I just thought "Bad slave, I will get by with trying to bleed it till I can afford to put another one in."   Since I was living with my girlfriend, and she had a car, and we both worked at the same place/same schedule, I didn't worry about it, just use her car.  Then, I bought a 87pathfinder July2000, so I was covered all around, and parked the fiero at my parents.   THEN THE FUN STARTS!  The Pathfinder blows the engine comming back from my brothers in Branson Mo.  I get fired from my job when I go in to work over BS.... then November 14th or 17th My girlfriend said shes leaving, and by 11 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">m that night, she had EVERYTHING moved out, (like a fool, I didn't want to be there while her friend, and mommy and daddy helped her pack) They took all the food, all the furnature, etc. All I had was my desk, computer, my clothes, and waterbed.  Next day, phone was shut off. &lt;anyway&gt; I stayed there 2 more weeks packing my stuff, and cleaning the totally trashed apt. Moved to my parents, and tried to figure out my Fiero. Would have to put in first, and start it because the clutch wouldn't engage at all now!  After replacing the slave, bleeding the heck out of it a billion time, removing the master, etc. I decided it was cheeper to fix the fiero then a new/rebuilt engine for the Pathfinder.  (I actually took my Fiero back to Sharps when it started not to engage, they told me it needed a new clutch, the master & slave held pressure.  I told them "I had you guys replace the clutch about a year and a half ago, spent $1200 bucks (USD)He said "well, this time its only going to cost you about 850 this time" I told them "Screw this, put it back together and I will deal with it myself" also spent 65 bucks for them just to look at it that time!. So I called all around and found this one place that told me "Sure we do Fiero Clutch replacements, I will tell you up front though, if your price shopping, then Im not going to be the cheepest, but we do it RIGHT the first time, and guarentee the parts and labor!"  Well, after several days of calling local area mech's and transmission specialist, I decided to take it to this one place that more or less told me "Come on down, check out our shop, I'll look at it etc., because I don't like to give phone estimates. Well, I took it down there, and the owner said the mechanics leave at 5:00 but he stays till 5:30 (I got there about 4:55) He took care of a few other people real quick, and about 5:20, I pulled it in. He got some tools, and we opened the back, and he watched me push the clutch, to see how much "push" was on the levers (we also seen the slave rod wasn't in the lever "cup" we spent 15-20 minutes taking the intake hose off, and loosening the slave to slip the rod back in place. I tried pushing the pedal again, no/little movement. I told him, I suspected the t/o bearing either pushed through the clutch fingers, or the clutch fork... he thought the slave, or master was bad. He got his power bleeder, and we bled the slave, still no lever movement. (also note that when all my problems started, a few weeks after it quit shifting/no clutch engagement, I noticed a noise when driving, then a week later no more bad noise) We stayed there till close to 7:00 looking at it, and I told him that I would bring it in tomorrow to drop it off so they could test it more. He opened the door, I put it in reverse, and started it... the bad noise from inside the traney was there again (ah ha, the rod/lever was pushing on something to make it do that) I backed up, and then he said "Yeah, I do hear that, your right, it is inside it, You want to leave it here, and I can take you home, that sounds pretty bad. I told him thats O.k. I would limp it home, and then just head back tomorrow, so I did. <BR>     Well, it took a month, and cost me $850 thats a new clutch set, new master, new seals, new clutch fork.  He kept all the parts for me to look at, told me what took so long, is that they thought there was a wire clip that fit the fork and t/o bearing. and after talking to the local pontiac dealer, and trying to figure out what the deal was (there was a paper included in the clutch kit that said Warrenty void without clip installed) but come to find out, it was talking about the 4speed clutch, and the 5 speed had the clip/wire  built in the 5speeed kit, or something.  The thing shifts smooth as silk, and the pedal is nice, smooth, and easy!  I have been driving the heck out of it because if its going to blow, then the at least I can get it taken care of! If anyone from SouthWest Missouri is reading this, and needs Fiero work done, this guy has been FANTASTIC so far, Super clean shop, will talk and show you everything. Heck, they cleaned and swept it out, and they cleaned and degunked the tranney, and under my shift console!!!!<P>Ask for Alex!!<BR>Moore Automotive<BR>3232 E. 32nd Street<BR>Joplin, MO.  64804 <BR>ph# (417)206-6200<BR>fax#(417)206-6262<P>Thanks Chance<BR>||||reg||4
