Z||000005||ChadMan||03-16-2001||08:59 AM||||He charged you $850 INCLUDING the master cylinder?  That's a pretty good deal!<P>Ah, Joplin...when my wife and I drove cross-country in my father-in-law's 86 SE, our only problem on the trip was a flat tire, which we had patched in Joplin.  When the mechanic saw the Ohio tags and heard we were on our honeymoon, he dropped what he was doing and patched the tire in 15 minutes, charging us $8.  What a guy!||||reg||14
Z||000006||bHooper||03-16-2001||09:22 AM||||i feel your pain... i've had that happen to me, in sequence (except for truck engine), several times.<P>btw, my finace's parents live in osage beach, on lake of hte ozarks... thats a neat place!<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000007||Chance||03-16-2001||09:29 AM||||Yeah Chadman, that was 850... including the Master Cyl, AND Clutch Fork, resurface flywheel, etc. etc. so I didn't think it was half bad considering.  Most other shops (and I called the transmission shops first) freaked when I said "Fiero" or wanted to charge a minimum of 300-400 for labor, could of been more.  I am hoping this is it for a while.  I was in Columbus Ohio in 86,87 or 88 for "SID Fest" (Commodore 64 days, Quantium Link was the hot online service, and 2400 baud was it. MIDI MUSIC and all that)<BR>Chance||||reg||7
