Z||000014||Chance||03-17-2001||01:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Kilodyne:<BR><B>Damn... Wish i had heard from you 2 weeks ago. Im Living in Pittsburg KS now and just got my car back from the shop with a clutch replacement on Thursday. I didn't get a bad deal though. $1000 for clutch replacement and A/C work parts and labor on waranty. <P>Chance- I was calling around Lots of salvage yards in the area looking for some fiero parts. I couldn't find anyone who had fieros. If you or anyone else out there knows where to find any good used parts in the South East Kansas, South West Missouri, North East Oklahoma area please let me know.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>     Yeah, wish you could of too... ypu might of saved a little money.  As for finding Fieros in the bone yards, It's slim pickings.  I kept checking around all the Joplin Yards for months and finally, this one place (Can't think of the name off hand but its on west 7th street here in Joplin with all the other Yards between Black Cat road and 66 speedway) they had got in 4 or 5 so at least its a start.  If you ever need a hand with your Fiero, or new to the 4 states and need the low-down on things, e-mail me... We could hit the Yards, not to mention I can call em' since its a local call for me.  <BR>Chance||||reg||14
Z||000015||Chance||03-17-2001||01:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KRMFiero:<BR><B>I am having that same problem right now, what was wrong with it, the bearing was pushed threw the fingers?  <P>Let me know ASAP<BR>Kyle</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The clutch fork where it holds the t/o bearing was bent so it wouldn't engage the clutch and things kind of all got "smushed" together so the slave pushrod or a crowbar wouldn't move the lever...||||reg||1
